{"text": "COMMONWEALTH of VIRGINIA\nOffice of the Attorney General\n\nKenneth T. Cuecinel 11 900 Bast Mai\n\u2018Atomey Genera Richmond, Virginia 2\n804-786\n\nFAX 804-786-1991,\nVirginia Relay Services\n800-828-1120\n\nAugust 9, 2013,\n\nAmy L. Austin, Esq.\n\u2018The Law Office of Amy L. Austin\n101 Shockoe Slip, Suite O\nRichmond, Virginia 23219\n\nRE: Appointment as Special Counsel to the Commonwealth of Virginia and\nVirginia Commonwealth University (SCA No. 2013-11)\n\nDear Ms. Austin:\n\nOn behalf of Virginia Attomey General Kenneth Cuccinelli, I, it is my pleasure to appoint you\nand your firm to serve as special counsel to Commonwealth of Virginia and Virginia Commonwealth\nUniversity. This appointment is pursuant to the Attorney General's grant of authority in \u00a7 2.2-507(\u00a2)\nof the Code of Virginia,\n\nThis appointment will commence as of the date of this letter, provided your acceptance is\nreceived by this Office within ten days and will continue through its completion, subject to the right of\nthe Office of the Attomey General to terminate the appointment at any time, with or without cause.\nThis Office reserves the right to assign or appoint other counsel on an as-needed basis.\n\nScope of Services\n\nYou and your firm are appointed to serve as special counsel to the Commonwealth of Virginia\nand Virginia Commonwealth University to represent the personnel of Virginia Commonwealth\nUniversity identified below for matters arising out of their testimony, interviews, or other inquiries",
